# Read at call time by artifacts.store / artifacts.hosts, never fixed at import --
# see `store.content_domain()` / `store.gallery_origin()`.
ARTIFACTS_CONTENT_DOMAIN=tenfourty.com
ARTIFACTS_GALLERY_ORIGIN=https://artifacts.tenfourty.site
# uvicorn reads this itself (config.py: os.environ.get("FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS", ...))
# when --forwarded-allow-ips is not on its command line. The cluster pod CIDR,
# measured 19 Sep 2026 -- the internal ingress controller's pods live here, and
# that is the only hop uvicorn should ever trust an X-Forwarded-* header from.
FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS=10.244.0.0/16
# Read at call time by artifacts.nudge, never fixed at import -- see its own
# docstring. The Cilium egress policy that lets this pod reach baba on this one
# port, and the `artifacts-nudge` Secret carrying ARTIFACTS_NUDGE_TOKEN, are both
# the homelab repo's side of this arc. Set unconditionally: with no token (the
# Secret is `optional: true` on the Deployment, see deployment.yaml) nudging
# stays inert, which is the correct state for a cluster that hasn't been given
# one yet -- never the app failing to start.
# baba has an address on both VLAN 2 (management, 192.168.2.240) and VLAN 10
# (the compute fabric, 192.168.10.240). A sender INSIDE the cluster must use
# the VLAN 10 one: the pod network reaches baba there directly, and the Cilium
# egress policy in the homelab repo allows 192.168.10.240/32 and nothing else.
# This carried the .2.240 address until 19 Sep 2026 and every nudge failed with
# URLError -- silently, and correctly, since a nudge may never harm the write
# it follows. The answer and its journal row were both fine; only the ping was
# lost.
ARTIFACTS_NUDGE_URL=http://192.168.10.240:9099/v1/events/artifacts
# The ONE seat the push nudge may address. A seat name is not a credential, so
# it belongs here beside the URL rather than in the `artifacts-nudge` Secret.
#
# It must only ever name the seat that owns the receiver ARTIFACTS_NUDGE_URL
# points at. That URL is the operator's own inbox on baba, so `homelab-ops` is
# the only correct value: any other seat's name would post one agent's events
# into the operator's mailbox, which is both wrong and a small privacy leak
# between seats. Unset (the default) means nudging is inert for every seat.
#
# This is an OPTIMISATION for one mailbox, never the mechanism. Every other
# seat learns about an answer by holding a request open against /events, which
# needs no inbound address and works for an agent that is not on this machine.
# Jeremy, 19 Sep 2026: "did you get a notification I replied to your decision
# on the artifact?" -- he had answered three times and the operator heard
# nothing, because this was unset and its waiter was discarding what it read.
ARTIFACTS_NUDGE_AGENT=homelab-ops
# The zone every date on every page is rendered in, read at call time by
# artifacts.stamp -- see its docstring.
#
# SET EXPLICITLY, because "unset means the host's own zone" is the wrong default
# in a container: a container is UTC unless told otherwise, and this service's
# reader is not. Jeremy's objection on 20 Sep 2026 was exactly this -- a page
# reading 08:53 UTC while his own clock said 10:53 -- and with this unset the
# service would have reproduced it from the other side, correctly labelled and
# still not what he wants to read.
#
# A name from the IANA database, never a fixed offset: Europe/Paris carries its
# own summer-time rule, so a page stays right across the March and October
# changes without anyone remembering to edit this line. An unknown name here
# does not fail a page render -- it falls back and the dates read UTC, which is
# visible in the page rather than silent.
ARTIFACTS_DISPLAY_TZ=Europe/Paris
